  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Ownership is derived, never stored",
      "items": [
        "The run-start line records which app spawned the run.",
        "The answers and artifacts routes re-derive that owner on every request.",
        "A restart never loosens the gate and never strands a run.",
        "router/server.js:1235 and 1921"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The journal is the record",
      "items": [
        "run.jsonl carries the phases, agent and tool calls, each escalation and its answer.",
        "summary.json closes the run and releases the spawn slot.",
        "Nothing in the plane is reconstructed after the fact.",
        "lib/workflow/engine.mjs:139 and 662 · lib/workflow/memory.mjs",
        "The memory plane is the tier above run.jsonl: durable across runs and agents (the memory capability)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "An escalation can hold for its owner",
      "items": [
        "A declared answer, then the live answers.jsonl row.",
        "Then a question-substring match against either.",
        "Then the owner wait (awaitOwnerMs): the run holds open and the human answers over the wire.",
        "Then askOwner, then a recorded \"no owner\" answer.",
        "The source that resolved it is journalled.",
        "lib/workflow/engine.mjs:953"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Agents ride the router",
      "items": [
        "The plane's model calls go back through 127.0.0.1:8300 with the operator token.",
        "Quota steering, failover, and the mixture still apply inside a workflow.",
        "Judgments route to sys1 for classification and to TypeSafe for decisions.",
        "lib/workflow/engine.mjs:105 and 551"
      ]
    }
  ]
